    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0196" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–3145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Chinese
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Vincent</hi>)<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d147-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-31">January 31, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There is attached a very useful memorandum prepared by Mr. Perkins<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d147-f2"/> with regard to advocated reforms in China. I asked Mr.
                    Perkins to prepare the memorandum with a view to having readily available
                    information to answer inquiries regarding what <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chinese</hi> consider to be needed reforms. You may also find the
                    memorandum useful in this respect.</p>
                <pb facs="0197" n="187" xml:id="pg187"/>
                <p>It is worthy of note that the political reforms advocated by non-Communist
                    Chinese organizations and individuals are in a very large measure the same
                    reforms that the Chinese Communist Party advocates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ohn</hi>] C[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >arter</hi>] V[<hi rendition="#small-caps">incent</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d147-a1.xml" xpointer="d147-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d147-f1" n="44" type="source" xml:id="d147-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Director of the Office of Far Eastern Affairs (Ballantine) and
                    the Under Secretary of State (Grew).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f2" n="45" xml:id="d147-f2-content">
                <p>Troy L. Perkins of the Division of Chinese Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
